// Fifty original supplementary maths problems. Append-only IDs preserve saved history.
const SENIOR_PROBLEMS=[
[10,'A garden has area 48 m². Its length is 2 m greater than its width. What is its width?',['6 m','8 m','4 m','12 m'],'w(w + 2) = 48, so (w + 8)(w − 6) = 0. The positive width is 6 m.'],
[10,'A 10 m ladder leans against a wall with its foot 6 m from the wall. How high up the wall does it reach?',['8 m','4 m','16 m','7 m'],'The height is √(10² − 6²) = √64 = 8 m.'],
[10,'A ramp makes a 30° angle with level ground and rises 2 m. Using sin 30° = 0.5, what is the ramp length?',['4 m','1 m','2.5 m','3 m'],'sin 30° = rise/ramp length, so the length is 2 ÷ 0.5 = 4 m.'],
[10,'A printer costs $180 plus 4 cents per page. Another costs $120 plus 6 cents per page. After how many pages do their total costs match?',['3000 pages','1000 pages','1500 pages','6000 pages'],'The $60 initial difference is offset by $0.02 per page: 60 ÷ 0.02 = 3000.'],
[10,'A savings account starts with $800 and earns 5% interest each year, compounded annually. Ignoring fees, what is its balance after 2 years?',['$882','$880','$840','$920'],'800 × 1.05² = 882. The second year earns interest on the first year’s interest too.'],
[10,'A machine worth $2000 loses 15% of its value each year. What is its value after 2 years?',['$1445','$1400','$1700','$1450'],'Multiply by 0.85 twice: 2000 × 0.85² = 1445.'],
[10,'A spinner has 5 equal sections, 2 blue and 3 red. It is spun twice independently. What is the probability of exactly one blue?',['12/25','4/25','6/25','9/25'],'Blue then red or red then blue: 2 × (2/5)(3/5) = 12/25.'],
[10,'A bag has 3 green and 5 yellow counters. Two are drawn without replacement. What is the probability of two yellow counters?',['5/14','25/64','5/8','3/8'],'Multiply 5/8 by 4/7: 20/56 = 5/14.'],
[10,'A model ball’s height is h = −t² + 6t metres after t seconds. What is its greatest height?',['9 m','6 m','12 m','18 m'],'Complete the square: h = 9 − (t − 3)², so the maximum height is 9 m.'],
[10,'A rectangle is enlarged with a length scale factor of 1.5. Its original area is 32 cm². What is the new area?',['72 cm²','48 cm²','64 cm²','96 cm²'],'Area scales by 1.5² = 2.25. Then 32 × 2.25 = 72.'],
[10,'A cone has radius 3 cm and height 8 cm. Using V = πr²h/3, what is its volume?',['24π cm³','72π cm³','8π cm³','18π cm³'],'π × 3² × 8 ÷ 3 = 24π cm³.'],
[10,'A circular garden has radius 5 m. A path extends to an outer radius of 6 m. What is the path area?',['11π m²','π m²','25π m²','36π m²'],'Subtract the garden area from the outer circle: π(6² − 5²) = 11π.'],
[10,'A delivery route joins A(−2, 1) to B(4, 9) on a grid measured in kilometres. What is the straight-line distance?',['10 km','14 km','8 km','12 km'],'The coordinate differences are 6 and 8. Distance is √(6² + 8²) = 10 km.'],
[10,'A data set has mean 14 for 8 values. Adding one value changes the mean to 15. What value was added?',['23','15','22','29'],'The old total is 112 and the new total is 135. The added value is 23.'],
[10,'A linear model predicts 12 litres of fuel for 150 km. At the same rate, how much fuel is needed for 425 km?',['34 L','30 L','36 L','38 L'],'The rate is 12/150 = 0.08 L/km. Multiply by 425 to get 34 L.'],
[10,'A club’s profit is P = 18n − 270 dollars for n tickets sold. What is the smallest whole number of tickets giving positive profit?',['16 tickets','15 tickets','14 tickets','18 tickets'],'Positive profit needs 18n > 270, or n > 15. The smallest whole number is 16.'],
[10,'A square’s side is measured as 12 cm to the nearest centimetre. What is the upper bound for its area?',['156.25 cm²','144 cm²','169 cm²','150 cm²'],'The side is less than 12.5 cm. Its area is therefore less than 12.5² = 156.25 cm²; this is the upper bound.'],
[11,'A population model is N(t) = 500 × 1.2^t. What is the predicted population after 3 time units?',['864','800','720','900'],'Multiply the starting population by the growth factor three times: 500 × 1.2³ = 864.'],
[11,'A culture doubles every 4 hours. It starts with 300 cells. How many cells does the model predict after 12 hours?',['2400','1200','3600','4800'],'Twelve hours contains three doubling periods: 300 × 2³ = 2400.'],
[11,'A logarithmic scale uses L = log₁₀(I). If I changes from 100 to 10,000, by how much does L increase?',['2','100','4','3'],'log₁₀(100) = 2 and log₁₀(10,000) = 4. The increase is 2.'],
[11,'A company models revenue as R(x) = 40x − x² dollars. At what x is revenue greatest?',['20','40','10','80'],'R(x) = 400 − (x − 20)², so the maximum occurs at x = 20.'],
[11,'A tank’s volume is V(t) = 5t² + 10 litres. What is its instantaneous filling rate at t = 3 minutes?',['30 L/min','55 L/min','15 L/min','45 L/min'],'V′(t) = 10t, so V′(3) = 30 L/min.'],
[11,'A moving object has position s(t) = t³ − 2t metres. What is its velocity at t = 2 seconds?',['10 m/s','4 m/s','12 m/s','6 m/s'],'Velocity is s′(t) = 3t² − 2. At t = 2, it is 12 − 2 = 10 m/s.'],
[11,'A line tangent to y = x² at x = 3 is used as a local model. What is its equation?',['y = 6x − 9','y = 3x','y = 6x + 9','y = 9x − 18'],'The slope is 2x = 6 and the point is (3,9). Thus y − 9 = 6(x − 3).'],
[11,'A sequence of savings deposits starts at $15 and increases by $5 each week. What is the total deposited over the first 10 weeks?',['$375','$600','$350','$300'],'The tenth deposit is $60. Sum = 10(15 + 60)/2 = $375.'],
[11,'A bouncing ball reaches 80% of its previous height each bounce. Starting at 2 m, what height follows the third bounce?',['1.024 m','1.28 m','0.8 m','1.6 m'],'Multiply the starting height by 0.8 for each of three bounces: 2 × 0.8³ = 1.024 m.'],
[11,'Of 40 students, 24 study music, 18 study drama and 10 study both. How many study neither?',['8','12','6','10'],'Music or drama includes 24 + 18 − 10 = 32 students. Thus 40 − 32 = 8 study neither.'],
[11,'Of 30 club members, 12 cycle to school. Of those 12, 9 wear reflective jackets. Given that a member cycles, what is the probability they wear a reflective jacket?',['3/4','3/10','2/5','1/3'],'Use the cycling group as the denominator: 9/12 = 3/4.'],
[11,'A game pays $12 with probability 1/4 and $0 otherwise. Entry costs $2. What is the expected net gain per play?',['$1','$3','$2','$10'],'Expected payout is 12 × 1/4 = $3. Subtract the $2 entry cost to get $1.'],
[11,'A trial succeeds with probability 0.3. Three independent trials are run. What is the probability of at least one success?',['0.657','0.9','0.343','0.027'],'Use the complement: 1 − 0.7³ = 0.657.'],
[11,'A triangular plot has sides of 8 m and 10 m enclosing a 30° angle. Using sin 30° = 0.5, find its area.',['20 m²','40 m²','80 m²','10 m²'],'Area = ½ab sin C = ½ × 8 × 10 × 0.5 = 20 m².'],
[11,'Two paths of lengths 5 km and 8 km meet at a 60° angle. Using cos 60° = 0.5, what is the distance between their far ends?',['7 km','13 km','9 km','√89 km'],'The cosine rule gives c² = 25 + 64 − 2 × 5 × 8 × 0.5 = 49, so c = 7.'],
[11,'Temperatures have mean 18°C and standard deviation 3°C. Each reading is converted using F = 1.8C + 32. What is the standard deviation in °F?',['5.4°F','37.4°F','3°F','1.8°F'],'Adding 32 does not change spread. Multiplying by 1.8 multiplies standard deviation by 1.8: 3 × 1.8 = 5.4.'],
[11,'A model height is h(t) = 4 + 3 sin(t), with t measured in radians. What is its range?',['1 to 7','−3 to 3','4 to 7','−7 to 7'],'Since sin(t) ranges from −1 to 1, h ranges from 4 − 3 to 4 + 3.'],
[12,'A particle has velocity v(t) = 3t² m/s for 0 ≤ t ≤ 2. What distance does it travel in this interval?',['8 m','12 m','6 m','4 m'],'Velocity is non-negative, so distance is ∫₀²3t² dt = [t³]₀² = 8 m.'],
[12,'Water enters a tank at rate 6t + 2 L/min for 0 ≤ t ≤ 3. How much water enters during those 3 minutes?',['33 L','60 L','27 L','24 L'],'Integrate the rate: [3t² + 2t]₀³ = 27 + 6 = 33 L.'],
[12,'A particle has velocity v(t) = 2t − 4 m/s for 0 ≤ t ≤ 4. What total distance does it travel?',['8 m','0 m','16 m','4 m'],'It changes direction at t = 2. Each triangular area under |v| is 4 m, giving 8 m total.'],
[12,'A rectangle is built against a wall using 40 m of fencing for the other three sides. What is its greatest possible area?',['200 m²','100 m²','400 m²','160 m²'],'For depth x, width is 40 − 2x. Area = 40x − 2x², maximised at x = 10, giving 200 m².'],
[12,'A cost model is C(x) = x³ − 6x² + 15x + 20. What is the marginal cost C′(2)?',['3','12','7','24'],'C′(x) = 3x² − 12x + 15. At x = 2, this is 12 − 24 + 15 = 3.'],
[12,'A population follows P(t) = 100e^(0.2t). What is its instantaneous growth rate at t = 0?',['20 per time unit','100 per time unit','0.2 per time unit','200 per time unit'],'P′(t) = 20e^(0.2t), so P′(0) = 20.'],
[12,'A quantity follows Q(t) = 80e^(−0.5t). At what time does it reach 40?',['2 ln 2','ln 2','4 ln 2','0.5 ln 2'],'e^(−0.5t) = 1/2, so −0.5t = −ln 2 and t = 2 ln 2.'],
[12,'A path is modelled by y = ln(x). What is the slope at x = 4?',['1/4','4','ln 4','−1/4'],'The derivative of ln(x) is 1/x. At x = 4, it is 1/4.'],
[12,'A signal is f(t) = sin(3t), with t in radians. What is f′(0)?',['3','1','0','−3'],'By the chain rule, f′(t) = 3 cos(3t). At zero, cos 0 = 1.'],
[12,'A positive function is f(x) = x e^x. What is its derivative at x = 1?',['2e','e','e²','1 + e'],'By the product rule, f′(x) = e^x + xe^x. At x = 1, this is 2e.'],
[12,'A random variable has density f(x) = 2x on 0 ≤ x ≤ 1. What is P(X > 0.5)?',['0.75','0.5','0.25','1'],'Integrate 2x from 0.5 to 1: [x²] = 1 − 0.25 = 0.75.'],
[12,'A random variable is uniformly distributed from 2 to 10. What is the probability it lies between 4 and 7?',['3/8','3/10','1/2','5/8'],'For a uniform distribution, probability is interval length divided by total length: (7 − 4)/(10 − 2) = 3/8.'],
[12,'A binomial variable counts successes in 20 independent trials, each with success probability 0.4. What is its variance?',['4.8','8','12','3.2'],'Binomial variance is np(1 − p) = 20 × 0.4 × 0.6 = 4.8.'],
[12,'Independent measurements have population standard deviation 12. What is the standard deviation of the sample mean for a random sample of 36?',['2','1/3','72','12'],'The standard error is σ/√n = 12/6 = 2.'],
[12,'A sample mean is 50 and its standard error is 2. Using the normal critical value 1.96, what is the approximate 95% confidence interval?',['46.08 to 53.92','48.04 to 51.96','48 to 52','42.16 to 57.84'],'The margin is 1.96 × 2 = 3.92. Add and subtract it from 50.'],
[12,'A quality test flags 90% of defective items and 10% of good items. If 20% of items are defective, what fraction of flagged items are defective?',['9/13','9/10','1/5','2/3'],'Out of 100 items, 18 defective and 8 good items are flagged. Thus 18/26 = 9/13 of flagged items are defective.']
];
for(const [i,[year,prompt,options,why]] of SENIOR_PROBLEMS.entries())addSenior(year,'Mathematics',prompt,options,why,'senior-problem-'+i);
